Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.10,0:00:03.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,The most expensive trade\Nusually isn't the loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.30,0:00:06.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,It's the one you take\Nright {\c&H1EB0F2&}after{\c&HFAF7F5&} it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.80,0:00:10.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,You lose. You feel it.\NTen minutes later,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:13.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,you're back in. {\c&H1EB0F2&}Bigger{\c&HFAF7F5&}\Nsize. Worse setup. No
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.20,0:00:13.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.90,0:00:16.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's {\c&H1EB0F2&}revenge{\c&HFAF7F5&} trading.\NThe fix isn't willpower.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.00,0:00:20.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,It's a rule you set\N{\c&H1EB0F2&}before{\c&HFAF7F5&} the loss happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.60,0:00:23.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,Here's mine. After a\Nfull stop-out, I close
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.80,0:00:27.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,the chart for fifteen\Nminutes and write down
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.00,0:00:28.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,what happened first.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.50,0:00:32.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,And any trade I take out\Nof frustration gets
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.10,0:00:35.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,tagged {\c&H1EB0F2&}revenge{\c&HFAF7F5&} trade.\NTag it, and you can see
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.70,0:00:37.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,what that feeling costs\Nyou.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.00,0:00:40.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,Follow for more {\c&H1EB0F2&}honest{\c&HFAF7F5&}\Ntrading habits.
